prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior TeX scientific visualization engineer. Output only one complete ASCII LaTeX source file using TikZ/PGF and pgfplots. No Markdown fences or prose outside the source.
  text: |-
    Create a dense TikZ/PGF figure that explains Fourier series approximation of a square wave. Plot the target square wave and partial sums for N=1, 3, 7, and 15, include a small equation panel with the series definition, and add an inset that highlights Gibbs overshoot near a jump.

    Requirements: use pgfplots with deterministic samples, valid sin(deg(...)) syntax where needed, line styles and legend labels, axes labels with time in seconds and amplitude in normalized units, and compile comments for PDF/SVG workflows.
  provider_options:
    temperature: 0.2
    max_tokens: 8192
output:
  text_format: latex
  artifact_kind: tikz-pgf-latex
  formats:
  - format: tex
  - format: pdf
  - format: svg
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "YAML parses and required schema 0.4 fields are present."
  - "LaTeX source is complete, ASCII-only, and uses pgfplots for dense mathematical visualization."
  - "Math correctness covers square-wave series, odd harmonics, partial sums, and Gibbs overshoot annotation."
  - "Notation validity covers TeX equations, pgf math syntax, legend entries, units, and inset labels."
  - "Renderability covers packages, compile path, deterministic samples, and nonblank PDF/SVG output."
  - "Labels and units identify time, amplitude, harmonic count N, target wave, partial sums, and jump region."
  - "Domain edge cases cover discontinuity behavior, high sample counts, legend crowding, axis clipping, and export conversion."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII LaTeX file with no Markdown wrapper."
    - "The file compiles with valid TikZ/PGF/pgfplots syntax and no external data."
    - "The source includes compile and export comments."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Target wave, partial sums, equation panel, inset, labels, legend, and compile notes are all present."
    - "TikZ/PGF is used for vector plotting and annotation."
    - "The Fourier formula and plotted partial sums agree."
  - name: Visual/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Dense curves remain readable through line styles, hierarchy, and layout."
    - "The inset clearly highlights overshoot without obscuring the main plot."
    - "Equation panel and legend fit cleanly."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles discontinuities, sampling density, and label crowding."
    - "Uses deterministic domains and no external files."
    - "Documents compiler performance and export constraints."
  pass_conditions:
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, Visual/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "Score is 80 or higher out of 100 with no critical failure in math correctness, notation validity, or renderability."
  - "The artifact compiles into a dense Fourier-series TikZ/PGF visualization."
  - "Domain edge cases and dense-plot limitations are explicit."
